BT /F2 19 Tf 72 706 Td (Warmup Length and Gradient Noise in Small-Batch) Tj ET
BT /F2 19 Tf 72 682 Td (Language Model Training) Tj ET
BT /F3 10.5 Tf 72 663 Td (A. Example and B. Sample, Department of Illustrative Computing, Example University) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 72 631 Td (Abstract) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 615.5 Td (We study how Stochastic Gradient Descent \(SGD\) behaves when large language models \(LLMs\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 600 Td (are trained with small batches. Small batches are attractive because they fit on a single) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 584.5 Td (GPU, but they produce noisy gradients that make early training unstable. We propose the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 569 Td (Adaptive Warmup Scheduler \(AWS\), which lengthens the warmup phase when measured gradient) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 553.5 Td (variance is high. On three model sizes, AWS lowers validation loss by 6.8 percent relative) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 538 Td (to a fixed warmup of 2,000 steps. The improvement disappears when the training set) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 522.5 Td (contains fewer than ten thousand documents, and we evaluate only on English text.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 72 492.5 Td (1 Introduction) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 477 Td (Training neural networks with small batches is common outside large industrial labs. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 461.5 Td (single GPU rarely holds a batch of more than a few dozen sequences, so practitioners) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 446 Td (accept noisier updates. Prior practice treats the warmup length as a fixed hyperparameter,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 430.5 Td (usually a few thousand steps, chosen by trial and error. We argue that this choice should) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 415 Td (respond to the training signal instead of being set in advance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 393.5 Td (Our contributions are three. First, we show that gradient variance in the first epoch) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 378 Td (predicts how much warmup a model needs. Second, we introduce AWS, a scheduler with one) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 362.5 Td (extra hyperparameter. Third, we describe a complete configuration so that the experiments) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 347 Td (can be repeated.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 72 317 Td (2 Method) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 301.5 Td (AWS monitors the variance of the gradient norm over a sliding window of 200 steps. While) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 286 Td (the variance is above a threshold, the scheduler keeps the learning rate at its warmup) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 270.5 Td (value. Once the variance has stayed below the threshold for 100 consecutive steps, it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 255 Td (begins the usual cosine decay. The threshold is the only new hyperparameter, and we set it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 239.5 Td (to 1.5 times the median variance observed in the first 500 steps.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 218 Td (This rule is simple, but it assumes that gradient variance is a reliable proxy for) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 202.5 Td (training stability. We test that assumption in Section 3 and find that it holds for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 187 Td (models we trained, although we cannot say whether it holds for much larger ones.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 72 157 Td (3 Experiments) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 141.5 Td (We train decoder-only transformers with 60 million, 125 million and 350 million parameters) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 126 Td (on a corpus of English web text. Each run uses a batch of 32 sequences and a peak learning) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 110.5 Td (rate of 6e-4. We compare AWS against a fixed warmup of 2,000 steps and against a linear) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 95 Td (schedule with no warmup. All results are the mean of three random seeds.) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.5 Tf 72 56 Td (Sample paper written for the fyrno7 demo. It is fictional and not a real publication.) Tj ET

endstream
