BT /F1 11 Tf 72 714.5 Td (AWS reaches a validation loss 6.8 percent lower than the fixed warmup at 125 million) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 699 Td (parameters, and 4.1 percent lower at 350 million. The no-warmup baseline diverged in two) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 683.5 Td (of nine runs. Training time per step increases by less than 1 percent, because the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 668 Td (variance is computed from statistics that are already available during the backward pass) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 652.5 Td (and adds negligible FLOPs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 631 Td (When we repeat the experiment with only 8,000 documents, the three schedules are) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 615.5 Td (statistically indistinguishable. We therefore recommend AWS only when enough data is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 600 Td (available for the early gradient statistics to be meaningful.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 72 570 Td (4 Limitations and conclusion) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 554.5 Td (Our evaluation uses English text only, and we did not measure downstream task accuracy.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 539 Td (The seed count is small, and the confidence intervals for the 350 million parameter model) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 523.5 Td (overlap with the baseline in one of three comparisons. We also tuned the threshold on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 508 Td (125 million parameter model and reused it elsewhere, which may favour that size.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 486.5 Td (Gradient variance is a cheap signal that lets a scheduler decide its own warmup. We expect) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 471 Td (the idea to transfer to other optimizers, but we have not tested that. Future work should) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 455.5 Td (cover multilingual data and larger models.) Tj ET
